Subject: [PATCH 2/3] blt-toasty: fix Slack timeout under Pyodide; share issue
 URL (#35)

Review follow-up. The 5 s timeout used setTimeout with a Python lambda;
Pyodide destroys that borrowed proxy when setTimeout returns, so a hung
Slack request would never be aborted. Use AbortSignal.timeout instead,
as blt-vanish's health check does, and add a test that drives the
Pyodide path with a fake js module.

Move the issue URL into forge_links.py so the notifier and mcp_export
build it the same way (this also restores the missing "/" in
mcp_export's source_ref). DEPLOYMENT.md now recommends a private
channel and says notifications start once #34 runs the triage stages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
